// sys/win, the pure part -- what every windowed demo's frame loop did between
// its native calls. The window itself (open, present, poll, close) belongs to a
// backend and waits for backends to link on demand (C7).
//
// Whether a polled event lets the loop go on: -2 is the window closing (or
// GFX_MAX_FRAMES reached), 27 is Esc, 113 is q. Five demos carried this as
// alive().
inp_live(int ev) {
  int hit = 1;
  if(ev = 0 - 2 || ev = 27 || ev = 113) {
    hit = 0;
  }
} return int hit;
(-2):(0)
(5):(1)

// One frame's pause at about 60 fps, then the next tick. Four demos carried
// this as advance().
sys_next(int n) {
  sleep_ms(16);
  int m = n + 1;
} return int m;
(0):(1)
(41):(42)
